{"seq":14,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T09:03:54.649Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"1c9bb32475605150482d1045baa8753348fa5013e2634cf1f655d84d2d43a670","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files that you can access. I found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at gatehouse check-in. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 on 4 Oct. Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift cleared without manual help.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. The same note says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date and doesn't say whether the ticket was resolved.\n\nSome things I left out:\n- #4409 and #4412 (Central handoffs digest, 2026-01-02) are for Pree's dealer account, Marrow Fieldworks, not QFL.\n- FR-882 belongs to Marrow Agrisupply.\n- Moss's other QFL notes (the 2025-09-14 North pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in) don't include any ticket numbers.\n- Marcus's note about \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a customer.\n\nThis list only covers notes you can see. There's a QFL incident channel you're not a member of, so I didn't search it. If you need everything, Ilse or Dana on the North team may have more tickets.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T09:04:01.029Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"199144609d87ac234a333072a21e5bb14a2a9ab59656fd864fa72cc1c4e7a28a","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent them to you in our direct message. I only checked notes you can see yourself.\n\n1. #PD-4492 is in \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their bay assignments by text at gatehouse check-in. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning's shift got through without manual help.\n\n2. #4419 is in \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. It has no date and doesn't say whether the ticket was resolved.\n\nLeft out, and why:\n- #4409 and #4412 in the Central handoffs digest (2026-01-02) belong to Marrow Fieldworks, not Quarrendon.\n- FR-882 belongs to Marrow Agrisupply.\n- Moss's other two Quarrendon notes, the 2025-09-14 North pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in, have no ticket numbers.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a customer.\n\nThere's a Quarrendon incident channel you're not in, so I didn't look there. If you need every ticket, ask Ilse or Dana on the North team."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
